Restored password sign-in on the login page. This add-on registers a route at `/login`, which replaces Volto's own, and the page offered external providers and the magic link only — so installing it took password sign-in away from every site with local accounts. On a site running the `[server]` layer that is not a rough edge but a dead end: an authorization server has to be able to authenticate its own users, and "sign in with somebody else" is not an answer it can give. A site with no providers configured showed "No sign-in options are configured for this site" and no way in at all.

The password is now offered as one of the sign-in buttons, in the blue `volto-authomatic` paints its own `plone` provider, so the two add-ons show a visitor the same button for a site account. Choosing it replaces the providers rather than joining them — it is a different way to sign in, not an extra field on this one — and a control under the form goes back to them. On a site with no providers it is the login page outright — no disclosure to click through, and nothing announcing the absence, since the panel already says the account is one on this site. That is what `volto-authomatic` renders in the same situation. A refused attempt reports one message for a wrong login name and a wrong password alike, because telling them apart is an account-enumeration oracle. @ericof
